    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0140" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg30"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/1827: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Nanking</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-22T18:00:00-04:00">September 22, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>75. Your 624, September 22, 3 p.m.<anchor n="37" xml:id="d34-f1"/> First, the
                    Secretary of State has not made the statement attributed to him; second, the
                    American Government was in no way consulted or informed in advance. You may so
                    inform your interlocutors.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d34-f1" n="37" xml:id="d34-f1-content">
                <p>Reference is to telegram from the Minister in China, <ref target="#pg26">p.
                        26</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
